      <h2>Our Audit Readiness Review</h2>
      <p>A focused engagement that leaves you with a central readiness record and a clear list of what to fix first.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps steps-5">
      <li class="step"><h3>Inventory</h3><p>Collect the compliance documents you currently have.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>Map</h3><p>Compare expected evidence with what exists.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>Identify</h3><p>Flag missing and stale materials.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>Prioritize</h3><p>Rank gaps and assign an owner to each.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>Record</h3><p>Establish a central readiness record you can maintain.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-m muted measure">When a matter calls for legal interpretation or representation, we recommend involving qualified healthcare counsel.</p>
